WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.060
When studies disagree, which answer should you trust?

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:08.860
Some report a large shift, others see little change, and a few lean the opposite

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:15.000
way. Simply counting which side has more studies treats noisy results like sharp

4
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:20.420
ones. Meta-analysis combines their measurements instead of counting votes.

5
00:00:23.333 --> 00:00:26.593
Before pooling numbers, you must gather studies fairly.

6
00:00:27.853 --> 00:00:32.853
That starts with a systematic review, a strict search for every study fitting preset

7
00:00:32.853 --> 00:00:38.553
rules. You set rules before seeing results, so you cannot cherry-pick favorite

8
00:00:38.553 --> 00:00:44.433
outcomes. Each matching study yields one comparable number, its effect size,

9
00:00:45.033 --> 00:00:46.653
measuring how big the change was.

10
00:00:47.767 --> 00:00:52.587
Each effect size also carries a horizontal bar showing its uncertainty.

11
00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:57.627
Stacked above one shared axis, these rows form a forest plot.

12
00:00:58.967 --> 00:01:02.847
A narrow bar means high precision, because random scatter is small.

13
00:01:04.087 --> 00:01:07.367
A wide bar means low precision and a noisy estimate.

14
00:01:08.467 --> 00:01:10.527
Precision sets each study's weight.

15
00:01:12.007 --> 00:01:15.627
Narrow bars earn large weights, and wide bars earn small ones.

16
00:01:17.027 --> 00:01:21.947
Multiply each effect size by its weight, sum them, and divide by the total weight.

17
00:01:23.527 --> 00:01:28.027
Meta-analysis weights studies by precision, so sharp measurements pull the pooled

18
00:01:28.027 --> 00:01:29.807
diamond more than noisy ones.

19
00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:32.950
Now test this rule on a forest plot.

20
00:01:34.390 --> 00:01:37.730
Most rows are noisy studies with wide bars near zero.

21
00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:41.770
Only a few rows have tight bars clearly to the right.

22
00:01:43.050 --> 00:01:47.310
If you weight by precision instead of counting votes, where does the pooled diamond

23
00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:48.310
land?

24
00:01:53.300 --> 00:01:55.460
The diamond lands clearly to the right.

25
00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:01.800
Although wide-bar studies outnumber sharp ones, large uncertainty shrinks each wide

26
00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:06.020
study's weight. A simple vote count would have missed the pattern.

27
00:02:07.100 --> 00:02:10.020
Still, pooling cannot rescue biased inputs.

28
00:02:11.280 --> 00:02:16.280
If studies with weak results stay unpublished, or one population dominates, the

29
00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:22.140
diamond tilts. Even clean trends across studies show correlation, not proof of

30
00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:28.400
cause. Reviewers guard against bias by setting search rules upfront, checking study

31
00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:30.340
design, and stating those limits.

32
00:02:31.433 --> 00:02:37.513
In 2011, I-Ching Chen, Chris D. Thomas and colleagues pooled published range shifts

33
00:02:37.513 --> 00:02:38.913
of terrestrial species.

34
00:02:40.333 --> 00:02:45.333
Shifts were greatest in studies whose regions had warmed most, a correlation across

35
00:02:45.333 --> 00:02:47.033
studies linking shifts to climate.

36
00:02:48.273 --> 00:02:53.613
In 2017, Pecl and colleagues reviewed evidence that climate-driven redistribution

37
00:02:53.613 --> 00:02:58.333
alters communities, ecosystem functioning, and human well-being.

38
00:02:59.517 --> 00:03:04.577
A 2014 review gathered plant transplant tests across range borders.

39
00:03:05.977 --> 00:03:11.037
In 46% percent of tests, the range limit matched a niche limit, where conditions

40
00:03:11.037 --> 00:03:12.197
turned unsuitable.

41
00:03:13.437 --> 00:03:19.297
In 26%, percent, mostly north-south or east-west limits, transplants survived beyond

42
00:03:19.297 --> 00:03:20.297
the range.

43
00:03:20.850 --> 00:03:26.270
In 23%, all at elevation limits, ranges ran past the niche limit.

44
00:03:27.530 --> 00:03:30.230
The shares do not add to 100%.

45
00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:36.050
Gathering every test turns scattered results into a clearer pattern than one study

46
00:03:36.050 --> 00:03:36.410
gives.
